      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Country Housewife and Lady\u0027s Director\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Prof. R Bradley, 1728 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#bradley-1728\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EBradley 1728\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EClary and Eggs,\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nTake eight or ten Eggs; beat them well in a Porringer; then take some Clary Leaves, and chop them small; add a little Pepper and Salt, and some Onion chopt small. This Mixture must be fry\u0027d in hot Lard or Hog-Seam, and serve it with Slices of Lemon.\u003Cbr\u003E"
